@using Lt2.SharedKernel
@inject Formats F

@* How a vote went, beside its numbers (design 8.18, "The majority"; owner, 2026-11-18). The open data carries no official
   outcome ("priimta", "pritarta") and the legal rule counts the MPs registered at the sitting, which is not stored, so the
   chip says the majority of those who voted, as the analytics page does (8.26.2, AnalyticsRules.SeimasMajority): "Dauguma
   už", "Dauguma prieš" or "Nėra daugumos"; a consensus is "Pritarta bendru sutarimu", the data's own words. A neutral chip:
   the word says it, and a vote without a majority for has the outlined chip (dashed when there is no majority at all), so
   they differ at a glance without colour. Nothing while the vote has no numbers. What it is, is one hint beside the list
   (MajorityHint), never one per row; the agenda's lists (the front page, /darbotvarke) carry none (owner, 2026-11-21). *@
@if (IsConsensus)
{
    <span class="tag tag--outcome" data-majority="consensus">@F.T["Consensus.Tag"]</span>
}
else if (HasResult && AnalyticsRules.SeimasMajority(new SeimasVoteNumbers(false, For, Against, Abstain)) is { } majority)
{
    <span class="@Class(majority)" data-majority="@majority">@F.T["Majority." + majority]</span>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool IsConsensus { get; set; }

    /// <summary>False until the per-MP results are read; the totals come with them.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool HasResult { get; set; } = true;

    [Parameter] public int? For { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public int? Against { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public int? Abstain { get; set; }

    private static string Class(string majority) => majority switch
    {
        SeimasMajorities.For => "tag tag--outcome",
        SeimasMajorities.Against => "tag tag--outcome tag--outline",
        _ => "tag tag--outcome tag--outline tag--dashed",
    };
}
